course: dictionary
lesson: 322
title: Angle: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence around it tells you which one to use. Angle is a good example. «Look at it from a different angle.» Here an angle is a way of thinking about something, not a shape. Ask yourself what the sentence needs the word to mean.
explain: In maths, an angle is the space or turn between two lines that meet at a point. We measure angles in degrees with a protractor. A right angle is 90°, like the corner of a box. An obtuse angle is bigger than a right angle, but less than a straight line.
explain: Angle can also be a verb. To angle something is to point it slightly sideways, as when you angle a lamp. To angle can also mean to fish with a rod and line. «A mirror reflects light at the same angle as the light arrives» uses angle as a noun for the slant of the light.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If you put in "pointed slightly sideways" and it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning. Phrases help too: «at an angle» means slanted, and «angle for» means trying to get something without asking for it directly.
fact: An angle is the space or turn between two lines that meet at a point.
fact: Angles are measured in degrees (°).
fact: A «right angle» is exactly 90°, like the corner of a box.
fact: A full turn is 360°, and the angles in a triangle add up to 180°.
fact: «From every angle» means from all sides, or in every way of looking at something.
exercise: «Look at it from a different angle.» What does angle mean here? | *A way of thinking about a problem | A fishing rod and line | A pointed corner made of two lines | A mirror in a bathroom
exercise: «A right angle is 90°.» How many degrees is a right angle? | 180 | 45 | 360 | *90
exercise: Dad says, «Angle the lamp a bit towards the desk.» What should you do to the lamp? | Carry it to the kitchen | Switch it off | Paint it blue | *Point it slightly sideways
test: What is the name for the space between two lines that meet at a point? | Shadow | Circle | Surface | *Angle
test: «Swim back in at an angle.» What does at an angle mean here? | Very fast | *Slanted, not straight | Straight down | Under the water
exam: «An obtuse angle is between 90° and 180°.» Which of these is an obtuse angle? | 90° | *100° | 45° | 360°
